    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-068 — Force Cairo CPU renderer.** Fixes the Wikipedia scroll segfault.\n\n**Production-verified 2026-11-03**: no crash on scroll, smooth performance, no visual regressions.\n\n## The crash\n\nGTK4's GSK GPU renderer crashes on very large cairo surfaces (~30,000px tall). Core dump backtrace:\n\n```\n#0  _cairo_clip_intersect_clip (clip=..., other=...) at cairo-clip.c:346\n#11 cairo_paint\n#12 gsk_render_node_draw (GskCairoNode)\n#15 gsk_gpu_upload_cairo_op_draw (stride=7356)\n#24 gtk_widget_render\n```\n\n**Zero HoneyBee frames** in the crash stack. Every frame from #11 onward is GTK4/GSK internal.\n\n## Why ADR-064 is the trigger\n\nBefore ADR-064: DrawingArea = 678px viewport height. Content below fold existed in layout tree but was never painted (cairo clipped small surface before GPU upload). Bug dormant.\n\nAfter ADR-064: DrawingArea = 30,447px full content height. GTK attempts to upload ~224 MB surface. Clip state corrupted → segfault.\n\nConsistent with \"had this segfault for a while\" — dormant since ADR-064, revealed by ADR-064's success.\n\n## The fix\n\n```cpp\nsetenv(\"GSK_RENDERER\", \"cairo\", 0);\n```\n\nOne line at top of `main()` before GTK init. `overwrite=0` preserves any user-set `GSK_RENDERER` so opt-in GPU testing remains available if a GTK fix lands.\n\n## Verified (production, user 2026-11-03)\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Scroll crash | Segfault (213 MB core) | **No crash** |\n| Scroll performance | Unreachable | **Smooth** |\n| Visual regressions | N/A | **None reported** |\n\n## What this unblocks\n\nADR-067 (JPEG verification) was blocked by this crash — the process never lived long enough to observe the Tim Berners-Lee photo.\n\n## What's deferred\n\n**ADR-069 candidate: viewport-clipped paint architecture.** Replace \"tall DrawingArea + ScrolledWindow\" with \"viewport-sized DrawingArea + scroll offset\" — real browser architecture, fixes the exposure at the source. ~200-300 lines, multi-session. Unnecessary until Cairo CPU becomes a bottleneck (currently smooth).\n\n## Test count\n\n691 / 2641 unchanged.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Production-visual, user-reported.**\n\nRefs #271\n",
